t  loose if his luck ever swings in the  opposite direction so it's  understandable why fry shamelessly  flaunts his wealth when the interest on  his thousand-year-old bank account makes  him a billionaire in season ones a fish  full of dollars now plenty of people  will tell you that taxidermy is in  pretty poor taste and collecting  skeletons really isn't much less creepy  and sure enough when fry pays ten  thousand dollars at an auction for the  skeleton of stalwart television actor  ted danson you've got to admit he's kind  of crossing a line fry's newfound ocean  of cash and pre-existing 90s nostalgia  coalesces into a turn of events that  introduces the evil company known as mom  corp danson's bones are only mentioned  in a one-off gag as fry says he needs  them because he's got an idea for a  sitcom but the fact that fry treats the  remains of a once living person like  this demonstrates exactly how far down  the rabbit hole he has fallen  anyone will tell you how much it sucks  to miss out on the finale of your  favorite show but when ler ruler of the  planet omicron persei 8 is prevented  from watching the last episode of single  female lawyer after a technical glitch  on earth he overreacts just a tad  the trajectory of events depicted in  season ones when aliens attack is set in  motion before the opening credits as fry  often ends up at the center of universe  altering events in futurama it tracks  that he was the one who spilled beer on  the late 90s fox control panel  eventually cutting off the broadcast  omicronians who are watching 1 000 light  years away  to extract his revenge and enforce his  will ler swoops down to earth and  immediately destroys the eiffel tower  the great sphinx of giza the leaning  tower of pisa and other prominent earth  landmarks he pulls off all of that in  pretty rapid succession too though  that's mostly because they've all been  relocated to the same beach in new new  york independence day eat your heart out  anyway ler 